  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "xmlParseNCNameComplex",
    "file": "libxml2/parser.c",
    "description": "xmlParseNCNameComplex computes a start pointer as `BASE_PTR + startPosition` before repeatedly calling `GROW` while scanning an NCName. `GROW` can reallocate/shift the input buffer, but the function keeps using the original base+offset-derived pointer when calling `xmlDictLookup(..., len)`. This can make the passed `name` pointer stale/out-of-bounds (pointing before current buffer), leading to out-of-bounds read in `xmlDictComputeFastKey` (crash site in dict.c).",
    "conditions": "In the schema harness, attacker-controlled schema bytes are parsed via `xmlSchemaParse -> xmlSchemaAddSchemaDoc -> xmlCtxtReadFile -> xmlParseDocument`. Input must drive `xmlParseNCNameComplex` (non-ASCII/complex NCName path) and trigger at least one `GROW` during name scanning so buffer relocation occurs. Then the final `xmlDictLookup` uses invalidated pointer with positive `len`, causing global-buffer-overflow read during dictionary hash computation."
  },
